function home():void{start('Universal time and local physical processes','Explore the ArcSecs universal-time premise, shared event deadlines, physical clock accumulation, biological change and measured gravitational redshift.','/universal-time/');localnav();?><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow gold">FOUNDATIONAL CLARIFICATION · 2.5.0</span><h1>Time is the When.<br><span class="gold">Physical processes are the change.</span></h1><p class="lead">Under the ArcSecs hypothesis, universal temporal progression is consistent everywhere. Gravity, motion and physical environments may affect atomic transitions, biological processes and other physical changes; they do not alter the underlying progression itself.</p></section><section class="tile"><h2>The exact charter</h2><p>Foundation 2: <strong>Time is constant.</strong></p><p>Foundation 4: <strong>Time does not physically exist; it is the “When.”</strong></p><p>Foundation 7: <strong>Spacetime does not physically exist.</strong></p><p>Time is an ordering parameter in this proposed interpretation, not a material substance. “Consistent everywhere” is a postulate about universal progression, not a claim that all physical clocks agree or that a preferred universal clock has been measured.</p><a href="/foundations/constant-time/">Original Foundation 2 lesson</a> · <a href="/foundations/when/">Original Foundation 4 lesson</a> · <a href="/foundations/spacetime/">Original Foundation 7 lesson</a></section><section class="section grid"><article class="tile"><span class="eyebrow gold">01 · THOUGHT EXPERIMENT</span><h2><a href="/universal-time/dinner/">Home in time for dinner</a></h2><p>Depart together at noon, experience distinct local clock and biological rates, and meet at the scheduled home-clock event. A six-hour reference interval need not produce six hours of local clock accumulation.</p><a class="button" href="/universal-time/dinner/">Run the dinner experiment →</a></article><article class="tile"><span class="eyebrow gold">02 · MEASUREMENT</span><h2><a href="/universal-time/benchmarks/">What do real clocks measure?</a></h2><p>Explore published optical-clock measurements and compare a reported signed gravitational redshift gradient with the relativistic reference and a stipulated candidate.</p><a class="button" href="/universal-time/benchmarks/">Inspect clock evidence →</a></article></section><section class="section grid"><article class="tile"><span class="eyebrow gold">03 · PHYSICAL RESPONSE</span><h2><a href="/universal-time/rates/">Compare process rates</a></h2><p>Inspect gravity and motion contributions to two candidate clock responses and a decay process against the conventional reference.</p><a class="button" href="/universal-time/rates/">Investigate rates →</a></article><article class="tile"><span class="eyebrow gold">04 · CAUSAL COMMUNICATION</span><h2><a href="/universal-time/synchronization/">Synchronize a remote clock</a></h2><p>Examine the bias introduced by asymmetric signal delays and the time remaining until a home-clock appointment.</p><a class="button" href="/universal-time/synchronization/">Investigate synchronization →</a></article></section><section class="tile"><h2>How the proposed interpretation differs from relativity</h2><p>Relativity assigns proper time to a worldline. Ideal clocks following different worldlines can accumulate different proper times between the same departure and reunion. General relativity does not require a material fabric, and generally does not provide a preferred universal simultaneity. The ArcSecs interpretation instead postulates a common progression T and regards clock accumulation as a physical response to local conditions.</p><p>Both pictures allow a reunion at the same dinner event with different clock readings. The analogy alone therefore cannot discriminate between them. A viable alternative needs quantitative rate laws, an operational synchronization procedure, causal consistency, agreement with the established tests, and independently falsifiable predictions. An appointment in a hypothetical separate universe also needs a physically specified communication and travel mechanism; the postulate does not guarantee that such travel is possible.</p><p>Read <a href="https://arcsecs.com/read-scientific-paper/">the scientific paper</a>, <a href="https://arcsecs.com/read-book/">the book</a> and <a href="/evidence/gates/">the open scientific validation gates</a>.</p></section><?php finish();}
function params(string $id):array{if(!$_GET)return [];return $_GET;}
function fmt(float|int $v):string{return abs($v)>0&&abs($v)<.0001?sprintf('%.6e',$v):rtrim(rtrim(sprintf('%.6f',$v),'0'),'.');}
function clock_label(float $hours):string{$seconds=(int)round(43200+$hours*3600);$day=intdiv($seconds,86400);$s=$seconds%86400;return sprintf('%02d:%02d:%02d',intdiv($s,3600),intdiv($s%3600,60),$s%60).($day?' (day +'.$day.')':'');}
function controls(string $id,string $path,array $r):void{?><form method="get" action="<?=h($path)?>" class="time-controls"><div class="grid"><?php foreach(catalog()['models'][$id]['parameters'] as $p):?><label class="tile time-field" for="time-<?=h($p['key'])?>"><?=h($p['label'])?><input id="time-<?=h($p['key'])?>" name="<?=h($p['key'])?>" type="number" required min="<?=h($p['min'])?>" max="<?=h($p['max'])?>" step="any" value="<?=h($r['parameters'][$p['key']])?>"><small>Allowed: <?=h($p['min'])?> to <?=h($p['max'])?></small></label><?php endforeach;?></div><div class="actions"><button type="submit" class="button">Calculate</button><a class="button secondary" href="<?=h($path)?>">Restore defaults</a></div></form><?php }
function chart(array $r):void{$rows=$r['rows'];$x0=$rows[0][0];$x1=$rows[count($rows)-1][0];$min=0;$max=0;foreach($rows as $row)foreach(array_slice($row,1) as $y){$min=min($min,$y);$max=max($max,$y);}if($max==$min)$max=$min+1;$x=fn($a)=>58+($a-$x0)/($x1-$x0)*615;$y=fn($a)=>245-($a-$min)/($max-$min)*200;$colors=['#ffd086','#82d7ff','#81d9ba','#c6afea'];?><div class="time-chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 700 300" role="img" aria-label="<?=h(implode('; ',$r['columns']))?>" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="0" y="0" width="700" height="300" rx="10" fill="#0b192b"/><?php for($i=0;$i<=4;$i++):$v=$min+($max-$min)*$i/4;?><line x1="58" x2="673" y1="<?=$y($v)?>" y2="<?=$y($v)?>" stroke="#45627e"/><text x="51" y="<?=$y($v)+4?>" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#c6d8e9"><?=h(fmt($v))?></text><?php endfor;foreach(array_slice($r['columns'],1) as $i=>$c):?><polyline stroke="<?=$colors[$i]?>" stroke-dasharray="<?=$i===2?'5 5':'none'?>" stroke-width="2.4" fill="none" points="<?=h(implode(' ',array_map(fn($a)=>round($x($a[0]),3).','.round($y($a[$i+1]),3),$rows)))?>"/><?php endforeach;?><line id="time-marker" x1="58" x2="58" y1="35" y2="245" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-dasharray="4 4" visibility="hidden"/><?php for($i=0;$i<=4;$i++):$v=$x0+($x1-$x0)*$i/4;?><text x="<?=$x($v)?>" y="264" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#c6d8e9"><?=h(fmt($v))?></text><?php endfor;?><text x="365" y="287" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e6f1ff"><?=h($r['columns'][0])?></text></svg><div class="chips"><?php foreach(array_slice($r['columns'],1) as $i=>$c):?><span class="time-legend time-legend-<?=$i?>"><?=h($c)?></span><?php endforeach;?></div></div><?php }
function result(array $r):void{?><section class="section tile"><h2>Calculated results</h2><?php if($r['model']==='dinner'):?><div class="time-clock-grid"><div class="time-clock"><span>HOME REFERENCE CLOCK</span><strong id="time-home-dial"><?=h(clock_label($r['metrics']['home_clock_hours']))?></strong><small id="time-home-acc"><?=h(fmt($r['metrics']['home_clock_hours']))?> accumulated hours</small></div><div class="time-clock"><span>TRAVELER'S CLOCK</span><strong id="time-traveler-dial"><?=h(clock_label($r['metrics']['traveler_clock_hours']))?></strong><small id="time-traveler-acc"><?=h(fmt($r['metrics']['traveler_clock_hours']))?> accumulated hours</small></div><div class="time-clock"><span>BIOLOGICAL PROCESS EQUIVALENT</span><strong id="time-bio-dial"><?=h(fmt($r['metrics']['biological_equivalent_hours']))?> h</strong><small>Illustrative reference-process accumulation</small></div></div><p class="meta">The clocks start aligned at noon. The traveler clock display is not a remotely synchronized home time. The final sample is the stipulated dinner reunion event.</p><?php endif;?><div class="stats time-stats"><?php foreach($r['metrics'] as $k=>$v):?><div><strong><?=h(fmt($v))?></strong><span><?=h(ucfirst(str_replace('_',' ',$k)))?></span></div><?php endforeach;?></div><?php chart($r);?><div id="time-interaction" hidden><label for="time-sample"><?=$r['model']==='dinner'?'Inspect progression':'Inspect multiplier sweep'?></label><input id="time-sample" type="range" min="0" max="<?=count($r['rows'])-1?>" value="<?=count($r['rows'])-1?>" step="1"><output id="time-readout" for="time-sample"></output><div class="actions"><button type="button" class="button secondary" id="time-json">Export JSON</button><button type="button" class="button secondary" id="time-csv">Export CSV</button></div></div><p class="meta"><?=h($r['limitation'])?></p><details><summary>Inspect numerical samples</summary><div class="time-table"><table><thead><tr><?php foreach($r['columns'] as $c):?><th scope="col"><?=h($c)?></th><?php endforeach;?></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($r['rows'] as $row):?><tr><?php foreach($row as $v):?><td><?=h(fmt($v))?></td><?php endforeach;?></tr><?php endforeach;?></tbody></table></div></details><script id="time-data" type="application/json"><?=j($r)?></script></section><?php }
function lab(string $id):void{$path='/universal-time/'.($id==='dinner'?'dinner':'benchmarks').'/';$error='';try{$r=calculate($id,params($id));}catch(\InvalidArgumentException $e){http_response_code(400);$error=$e->getMessage();$r=calculate($id);}start($id==='dinner'?'Home in time for dinner':'Atomic-clock observations and benchmarks',$id==='dinner'?'Shared departure and reunion with different clock and biological process rates.':'Published optical-clock frequency observations and a conditional numerical comparison.',$path,!!$_GET);localnav();if($id==='dinner'):?><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow gold">UNIVERSAL TIME · CONDITIONAL THOUGHT EXPERIMENT</span><h1>Home in time for dinner.</h1><p class="lead">If two people depart at noon and reunite when the home clock reads 6 PM, their clock and biological accumulations may differ. Under the ArcSecs premise, the underlying universal progression remains the same.</p><p>Choose the duration to the home-clock appointment and the fractions of that interval in two different physical environments. The home clock is set to one reference hour per hour of proposed progression. The model assumes the journeys meet the scheduled deadline; it does not derive a feasible trajectory or instantaneous communication.</p><p>Clock accumulation: N(T)/ν₀ = ∫ r<sub>clock</sub>(T) dT. Biological change: B(T) = ∫ r<sub>bio</sub>(T) dT. The biological quantity is an illustrative equivalent reference-process duration, not a prediction of lifespan or physiological aging.</p></section><?php else:?><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow gold">PUBLISHED OBSERVATIONS · CLOCK BENCHMARKS</span><h1>Measure the clocks. Test the explanation.</h1><p class="lead">Atomic-clock comparisons establish differences in accumulated readings and fractional frequencies. The ArcSecs hypothesis must reproduce these measured quantities. A different interpretation of time is not itself a quantitative prediction.</p></section><div class="grid"><?php foreach(catalog()['observations'] as $o):?><article class="tile"><span class="eyebrow"><?=h($o['year'])?> · <?=h($o['kind'])?></span><h2><?=h($o['title'])?></h2><p><?=h($o['summary'])?></p><a href="<?=h($o['url'])?>">Publication or institution ↗</a><p class="meta">DOI <?=h($o['doi'])?></p></article><?php endforeach;?></div><section class="section"><h2>Compare the published 2023 gradient</h2><p>All gradient quantities below use units of 10⁻¹⁹/cm. The source's sign convention is preserved. The conventional value is the authors’ reported reference (near Earth, the magnitude is approximately g/c²). A candidate multiplier of 1 reproduces the reference by construction, while 0 represents no gradient. Neither value derives the ArcSecs microscopic mechanism. A residual divided by the quadrature uncertainty is an illustrative comparison only.</p></section><?php endif;if($error):?><p role="alert" class="tile">Invalid input: <?=h($error)?>. Defaults displayed.</p><?php endif;controls($id,$path,$r);if($id==='dinner'):?><section class="tile"><h2>The shared appointment</h2><p>Home deadline: <strong><?=h(fmt($r['metrics']['home_deadline_hours_after_noon']))?> hours after noon</strong>. Traveler's accumulated clock hours: <strong><?=h(fmt($r['metrics']['traveler_clock_hours']))?></strong>. Both are present at the same reunion event by stipulation, regardless of clock count or biological-process equivalent.</p></section><?php endif;result($r);?><section class="tile"><h2>What remains to be explained?</h2><p>A physical universal-time theory needs a derived response for gravity, motion, different atomic transitions, particle decay, and other processes, not merely individually chosen rates. If it predicts exactly the same observations as relativity, this experiment alone cannot distinguish the interpretations. A common global ordering also requires a specified synchronization and causality prescription.</p><a href="/foundations/constant-time/">Foundation 2</a> · <a href="/visualizations/clocks/">Existing clock comparison</a> · <a href="/experiment-design/">Design a numerical test</a> · <a href="/evidence/gates/">Open validation gates</a></section><?php finish();}
